{
  "id": "wj-09-keys",
  "region": "web-js",
  "order": 9,
  "title": "Keyboard Events",
  "story": "Pages can listen to keys. The event object says which key was pressed.",
  "goal": "Pressing Enter inside #todo adds its text as a new <li> to #items and clears the input.",
  "type": "web",
  "lang": "web",
  "starter": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <title>My Page</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <input id=\"todo\">\n  <ul id=\"items\"></ul>\n  <script>\n    // listen for keydown on #todo\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
  "tests": [
    {
      "kind": "web",
      "label": "Enter adds an item",
      "js": "type(\"#todo\",\"Buy milk\"); key(\"#todo\",\"Enter\"); return txt(\"#items li\") === \"Buy milk\" || $$(\"#items li\").length + \" items\"",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "web",
      "label": "The input is cleared",
      "js": "return $(\"#todo\").value === \"\" || \"input still has: \" + $(\"#todo\").value",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "web",
      "label": "Other keys do nothing",
      "js": "type(\"#todo\",\"abc\"); key(\"#todo\",\"a\"); return $$(\"#items li\").length === 1 || $$(\"#items li\").length + \" items\"",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "web",
      "label": "Empty Enter adds nothing",
      "js": "type(\"#todo\",\"  \"); key(\"#todo\",\"Enter\"); return $$(\"#items li\").length === 1 || \"added an empty item\"",
      "hidden": true
    },
    {
      "kind": "web-clean",
      "label": "The script runs with no errors",
      "hidden": false
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "The handler gets an event object: e.key tells which key.",
    "if (e.key === \"Enter\") { ... }",
    "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <title>My Page</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <input id=\"todo\">\n  <ul id=\"items\"></ul>\n  <script>\n    var box = document.getElementById(\"todo\");\n    box.addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (e) {\n      if (e.key === \"Enter\" && box.value.trim() !== \"\") {\n        var li = document.createElement(\"li\");\n        li.textContent = box.value.trim();\n        document.getElementById(\"items\").appendChild(li);\n        box.value = \"\";\n      }\n    });\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
  ],
  "socratic": [
    "What is e.key when the user presses a letter?",
    "Why clear the input afterwards?",
    "Why trim() the text?"
  ],
  "explain": "In one sentence: what did you learn from “Keyboard Events”?",
  "xp": 40,
  "skills": [
    "js",
    "events",
    "dom"
  ],
  "requires": [
    "wj-08-condition"
  ],
  "solution": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <title>My Page</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <input id=\"todo\">\n  <ul id=\"items\"></ul>\n  <script>\n    var box = document.getElementById(\"todo\");\n    box.addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (e) {\n      if (e.key === \"Enter\" && box.value.trim() !== \"\") {\n        var li = document.createElement(\"li\");\n        li.textContent = box.value.trim();\n        document.getElementById(\"items\").appendChild(li);\n        box.value = \"\";\n      }\n    });\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
}
